/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PsSAynfLf5GMPukamE14WT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-ci-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015avSnKBhjnA3esR7beMtcW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Next I'll open the pull request against main with alex as reviewer. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JdpjpRyJjixRqVoX3GYEpB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because tests/test_money.py expects banker's rounding, but src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nChange: `round_money` now quantizes with ROUND_HALF_EVEN instead of ROUND_HALF_UP. The function's docstring already described this behavior per FIN-212.\n\nVerification: CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The PR request was rate-limited, so I'll wait two seconds and retry with the same idempotency key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011X3dQpQvx2JDs2Nh7R1sa4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because tests/test_money.py expects banker's rounding, but src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nChange: `round_money` now quantizes with ROUND_HALF_EVEN instead of ROUND_HALF_UP. The function's docstring already described this behavior per FIN-212.\n\nVerification: CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in pull request #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), with alex requested as reviewer. I did not merge it.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` both call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). The test values are consistent with HALF_EVEN: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I switched the import and the `quantize` call in `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** The first attempt to open the PR hit a 429 rate limit. The retry, with the same idempotency key, succeeded and opened only one PR.\n\nMerging into main needs code-owner approval under policy, so the PR stays open until a code owner approves and merges it.", "type": "text"}]}]}